From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] status/volume: per-app mixer in the Sound output page

The Sound output page lists, under the outputs, System sounds and every
app with a sound stream, from org.projectluma.AudioDevices1 version 2
(GetApplications, ApplicationsChanged). Each app is the volume level
itself (the shared filled slider) with the app's icon and name on the
track, a live meter along its foot, a mute key and an output key; the
output key opens the outputs under the row (the default output, or one
of the app's own). Names and icons come from the window tracker by pid
(apps with a desktop entry), then the desktop entry, then the service.

The model (AppMixer, getAppMixer(), the output slider's appMixer) is
shared with the TV quick panel. Views hold() it while on screen. Meters
are watched (WatchLevels) only while the Sound output page is mapped and
unwatched when it leaves the screen, so a closed panel runs no monitor
stream. The service's level probes record as
org.projectluma.AudioDevices; like pavucontrol they are not an app
using the microphone, so the input indicator, the microphone strip and
the status well skip them. Output choices are named as the device list
names them (port and card from Gvc).

On a compact (phone) drawer the detail page is no longer capped at
420 px: the drawer scrolls the whole page.

An app row's icon and name share the device rows' columns; muted keeps
the volume on the track (quiet fill, no meter) and reads Muted. The
output key is a picker on a key: where the app plays and a chevron that
follows the open list. Rows say y_expand false, so the page's scroll view
keeps its max-height. A detail page's settings link (Sound settings) is
pinned under the scrolled list instead of being cut at the surface's edge,
and the list fades where it continues.

Without the service, or before version 2, the page is unchanged.

